Match peer applications in cdp on the Application-Id alone.

RFC 6733 5.3: "The value of the Vendor-Id AVP in the
Vendor-Specific-Application-Id MUST NOT be used during computation." cdp
stored a peer's applications with the Vendor-Id they came in (0 for a plain
Auth-Application-Id, the group's Vendor-Id for one inside
Vendor-Specific-Application-Id) and routed only to a peer with the same
pair. TS 29.214 5.2 requires the PCRF to advertise Rx inside
Vendor-Specific-Application-Id, so the P-CSCF's STR, which carries a plain
Auth-Application-Id, found no peer: every STR (call end, de-registration,
after an ASR) was never sent, and ims_qos waits for the STA to tear down.

- Routing matches the application id only. That also drops the Vendor-Id
  that leaked from the Vendor-Specific-Application-Id step into the
  top-level one.
- The Destination-Host shortcut checked application 0 with vendor 0, so it
  never matched; it now checks the header's Application-Id, or relay.
- Process_CER() had the same pair compare, so a peer advertising Rx plainly
  to us configured with vendor 10415, or the reverse, got 5010
  DIAMETER_NO_COMMON_APPLICATION.

